===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[enroll]] as a [[member]] of a [[body]], especially of a [[college]] or [[university]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|by extension|often with '''to'''}} To [[join]] or [[enter]] (a [[group]], [[body]], [[category]] of [[people]], etc.).
#* {{quote-web|en|work={{w|Human Rights Campaign|HRC Foundation}}|title=Talking About Pronouns in the Workplace|url=https://hrc-prod-requests.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/files/assets/resources/TalkingAboutPronouns_onesheet_FINAL.pdf|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241129234651/https://hrc-prod-requests.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/files/assets/resources/TalkingAboutPronouns_onesheet_FINAL.pdf|archivedate=29 November 2024|accessdate=30 November 2024|text=As LGBTQ and ally-identified students '''matriculate''' to the workforce, many will come with an understanding of the importance of honoring personal pronouns and allowing for gender-inclusive pronouns such as "they, them, theirs."}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|stative}} To [[be]] [[enroll]]ed as a [[member]] of a [[body]], especially of a [[college]] or [[university]].
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Sean O'Connor|authorlink=Sean O'Connor (comedian)|actor={{w|Mary Mack (comedian)|Mary Mack}}|role=Jesse|episode=The Lavatic Reactor|title={{w|Solar Opposites}}|url=https://www.hulu.com/watch/4a6ddda0-cdf1-4ccc-a242-f820ea290fd4|season=1|number=5|date=May 8, 2020|time=7:45|text=“Saying this goes against every fiber of my brotherness, but you know what we have to do.” “Knife fight!” “No, we can't hate each other like siblings. We have to hate each other academically. We have to be each other's teachers.” “Well, then look to your left and look to your right, motherfucker, 'cause I'm about to '''matriculate''' your ass.”}}

